mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — growth diagnoses\n\nWorked diagnoses showing the loop, the broken-stage call, and the routing — plus honest\nexpectations. Subject: a solo founder building a SaaS social scheduler. Voice context is the blunt\nindie-founder voice; your output uses the loaded `voice.md`, `social-strategy.md`, `audience.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Diagnosis 1 — \"I post but get no reach\"\n\n**Signals (from native Insights):** most posts are photos/carousels; few Reels; low non-follower\nreach; hooks start slow; some Reels still have a TikTok watermark.\n**Broken stage:** **Reach.** Not enough Reels (the discovery engine), weak 3-second hooks, and the\nwatermark trips the originality gate.\n**Prescription:**\n- Shift the mix toward **Reels** for non-follower reach. → `reels-script`, `hook-writer`.\n- **Remove TikTok watermarks**; post native, made-for-IG versions. → originality gate.\n- Tighten the **niche** so the algorithm can categorize and recommend the account.\n- Keep carousels for saves/authority, not as the reach engine.\n→ Re-check **non-follower reach** and **watch time** in Insights in a few weeks.\n\n## Diagnosis 2 — \"Thousands of views, almost no new followers\"\n\n**Signals:** strong Reel reach and views; follower count barely moves; profile is a vague bio + a\ngeneric name field.\n**Broken stage:** **Follow-conversion.** Reach is fine; the **profile isn't converting** the visits.\n**Prescription:** this isn't a content problem — it's the profile. → `profile-optimization` (the\n3-second test, a searchable name field, a who/what/why bio, a goal-matched link, pinned posts). More\nviews won't help until the profile converts.\n\n## Diagnosis 3 — \"Decent followers, but nothing travels and they don't engage\"\n\n**Signals:** okay follower count; low **sends per reach**; quiet Stories; little community\ninteraction.\n**Broken stage:** **Sends + retention.** Content gets seen but isn't *send-worthy*, and the warm\naudience isn't being nurtured.\n**Prescription:**\n- Engineer **send-worthy** content (relatable / useful / conversation-starting). → `the-sends-lever.md`,\n  `viral-reverse-engineering` (what already gets shared in the niche).\n- Use **Stories** (polls, questions, replies) to deepen relationship and prompt DMs. → retention.\n- Reply fast to comments/DMs (early signals on each new post).\n→ Track **sends per reach** (aim past ~1–2%) and Story replies.\n\n---\n\n## Honest expectations (say this)\n\n- **Growth compounds; it's not a hack.** One viral Reel doesn't build a business; a converting\n  profile + send-worthy content + retention + consistency does.\n- **Follower count is vanity.** Track **reach, sends-per-reach, saves, profile visits, and leads** —\n  the things tied to actual outcomes.\n- **No guarantees.** You can stack the odds (hook + sends + niche + profile), not guarantee virality.\n- **No shortcuts.** Bought followers and pods are fake engagement that hurt reach and risk the\n  account.\n- **No WoopSocial analytics** — all of the above is read from **native Instagram Insights** the user\n  pulls, or qualitative review.\n\n---\n\n## What the diagnoses share\n\n- They name **one broken stage** of the loop, not a generic tip list.\n- They **route to the specific skill** that fixes that stage.\n- They center **Reels for reach** and **sends for travel**.\n- They set **honest, compounding expectations** and **vanity-free metrics**.\n"
